[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged **412 reports** as one issue and marked it known. Read by
tenant (locale and booking form), not by intake tag, they are two problems.

<Callout>
Not one issue. One fix queued covers only the larger of two.
</Callout>

## The two problems

| Problem | Reports | What it is |
|---|---|---|
| `parser` | 379 | The shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants get flipped dates. Affects all 11 tenants. |
| `hint` | 33 | `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, so day-first people type month first. A form bug, not a parser bug. Affects alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour. |

379 + 33 = 412. Five of the 379 (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620) are one-day moves, not month flips: likely a time zone bug. The desk files them under `parser` by tenant and footnotes them there.

## What the counts rest on

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

- The export repeats 15 reports across overlapping pages. One id is one report.
- Intake tags are wrong for 38 reports: 23 tagged `hint` are `parser`, 15 tagged `parser` are `hint`.
  Only the tenant's locale and form say which.

## What changed

The desk now merges on cause, not subject: [decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause)
replaces 0001, and the [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) follows it. Tickets: #1 (`parser`, 379),
#2 (`hint`, 33), both closed by pull request #4.

## Lessons

- Merging on subject alone (decision 0001) hid a second problem inside one count.
- A fix for the parser will not fix `booking-v3`.

